hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27898","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, that Salih, meaning Abu al-Khalil, narrated to him, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, that Umm Hakim bint al-Zubayr narrated to him that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr and tore a piece of shoulder with his teeth with her, then prayed and did not perform ablution from that."
"27899","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salih Abu al-Khalil, from Abdillah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Umm Hakim bint al-Zubayr, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her sister Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr and tore a piece of shoulder with his teeth, then stood for prayer and did not perform ablution. My father said: And al-Khaffaf said: She is Umm Hakim bint al-Zubayr."
"27900","Mu'adh, meaning Ibn Hisham, narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Umm Hakim bint al-Zubayr, that she handed the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a shoulder of meat, so he ate from it, then prayed."
